.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt CAT 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm cat
.Nd copy file or stream bytes to standard output
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Copy each named file in order, without text conversion, headers or numbering.
Relative paths use the working directory.
With no operands, read standard input; an operand
.Ql -
reads standard input at that point in the sequence.
.Pp
Input errors are reported on standard error; processing continues with the
next operand.
Output failure ends the command immediately.
A broken pipe, as when
.Xr head 1
has read enough, ends quietly with status 1: ABSD has no SIGPIPE.
Other output failures are diagnosed once.
.Pp
There are no options, including no
.Fl n
or
.Fl Fl help .
Options precede operands; a later option word is a path.
.Ql --
ends option processing; use it or a
.Ql ./
prefix for a name beginning with a dash.
Unknown leading options return status 2.
.Pp
Only files visible through this process's filesystem view can be opened.
The command changes no file itself.
Redirection is performed by the shell and requires writable destination
authority; it can truncate the destination before cat starts.
Do not redirect onto a file also being read.
For a durability barrier after a redirected write, see
.Xr sync 1 .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 if all input was copied and output flushed; 1 for an input or output
failure; 2 for an unknown leading option.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cat /etc/network.conf
echo middle | cat /etc/motd -
cat /etc/motd > /home/operator/motd
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr absd-sh 1 ,
.Xr head 1 ,
.Xr sync 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7
